# RCL-free component packages of github.com/redpanda-data/connect/v4.
#
# Derived from a static import-graph closure over connect v4.110.0: 55 of its 79
# public/components packages reach no file carrying the Redpanda Community
# License header, and 54 of those 55 can be linked into a shared library. The
# taint is transitive and NOT predictable from a package name --
# `snowflake`, `kafka`, `aws` and `redpanda` are all tainted, while
# `gcp` is clean because RCL there is confined to `gcp/enterprise`, which
# components/gcp does not import.
#
# Two single upstream files carry almost all the blast radius:
#   internal/serviceaccount/oauth2.go -> blocks a2a all aws cloud community
#                                        kafka ockam otlp redpanda
#   internal/license                  -> blocks a2a all aws cloud community
#                                        gateway google iceberg jira mssqlserver
#                                        mysql oracledb otlp postgresql
#                                        salesforce snowflake splunk
#
# tigerbeetle is RCL-free but absent: it ships prebuilt static archives, and
# neither links into -buildmode=c-shared. The macOS one has members that are not
# 8-byte aligned, which only the deprecated -ld_classic accepts; the Linux one
# carries R_X86_64_TPOFF32 initial-exec TLS relocations, which a shared object
# cannot hold and which we cannot recompile away.
#
# An entry may carry a Go build constraint after whitespace, which excludes it
# from platforms where it cannot link. Paths are relative to
# github.com/redpanda-data/connect/v4/public/components/.
# Regenerate with `go generate ./...` from go-bridge/ after editing.
# Verify with scripts/check-rcl.py, which reads the closure the compiler
# actually sees rather than trusting this list.

